ges L209:   * cite54†RSS feed L210: \nL211: cite55†Image: I/O logo†storage.googleapis.com L212: \nL213: May 19, 2026\nL214: # I/O 2026\nL215: \nL216: * * *\nL217: \nL218: At Google I/O 2026, we shared how we’re making AI more helpful for everyone.\nL219: \nL220: We’re releasing two new models, Gemini Omni and Gemini 3.5. Gemini Omni can create anything from any input, starting with video, and is a leap forward in world understanding, multimodality and editing, while Gemini 3.5 Flash is the first in our latest family of models combining frontier intelligence with action.\nL221: With advancements to Google Antigravity, our agent-first development platform, we’ve moved beyond AI tools that just help us write, to agents that help us act. Thanks to these agents, now anyone can be a builder.\nL222: \nL223: We’re unlocking agents and agentic experiences across our products — like with Information agents in Search, Gemini Spark and Daily Brief in the Gemini app and the launch of Universal Cart, a truly intelligent shopping cart.\nL224: And we’re continuing to scale Gemini across our products as well, from Google Pics to intelligent eyewear to Ask YouTube, creating new experiences and expanding to new form factors.\nL225: \nL226: Read on to learn more about what’s new.\nL227: \nL228:   *   *   *   *   *   *   *   *   *   *   *   *   *   *   *   *   *   *   *   *   *   *   *   *   *   *   *   *   *   *   * Explore more articles\nL229: \nL230:   * Privacy\nL231:   * Terms\nL232:   * Help\nL233:   * [Select]\nL234: \nL235:   * [Select]\n"
